{
 "title": "Why the Pythagorean Theorem Works",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The Right Triangle",
   "say": "Let's start with a right triangle having legs a and b, and hypotenuse c.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "Why Does a² + b² = c² Work?",
     "size": 52,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t0_shape",
     "d": "M 200 320 L 200 200 L 360 320 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "t0_right_angle",
     "d": "M 200 295 L 225 295 L 225 320",
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 2
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "t0_lbl_a",
     "x": 170,
     "y": 245,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "t0_lbl_b",
     "x": 270,
     "y": 335,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "t0_lbl_c",
     "x": 300,
     "y": 235,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "intro_text",
     "x": 500,
     "y": 230,
     "text": "We want to prove that the area c²\nequals the sum of areas a² and b².\nLet's use a visual rearrangement proof!",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Build Two Identical Squares",
   "say": "Imagine two identical large squares, each with side length a + b.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "erase",
     "ids": [
      "t0_shape",
      "t0_right_angle",
      "t0_lbl_a",
      "t0_lbl_b",
      "t0_lbl_c",
      "intro_text"
     ]
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq1_outer",
     "x": 160,
     "y": 200,
     "w": 400,
     "h": 400,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq2_outer",
     "x": 840,
     "y": 200,
     "w": 400,
     "h": 400,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq1_title",
     "x": 360,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "Square 1: Side (a + b)",
     "size": 32,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq2_title",
     "x": 1040,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "Square 2: Side (a + b)",
     "size": 32,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq1_top_a",
     "x": 220,
     "y": 165,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq1_top_b",
     "x": 420,
     "y": 165,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq2_top_a",
     "x": 900,
     "y": 165,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq2_top_b",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 165,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "gray"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Pack 4 Triangles in Square 1",
   "say": "In the first square, place four copies of our triangle around the edges. A tilted square with side c appears in the center.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq1_t1",
     "d": "M 160 200 L 280 200 L 160 480 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq1_t2",
     "d": "M 280 200 L 560 200 L 560 320 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq1_t3",
     "d": "M 560 320 L 560 600 L 440 600 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq1_t4",
     "d": "M 440 600 L 160 600 L 160 480 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq1_center",
     "d": "M 280 200 L 560 320 L 440 600 L 160 480 Z",
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq1_center_lbl",
     "x": 360,
     "y": 380,
     "text": "Area = c²",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq1_hyp",
     "x": 225,
     "y": 320,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rearrange 4 Triangles in Square 2",
   "say": "In the second square, pair the four triangles into two rectangles in the corners. The leftover space splits into two squares: a² and b².",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq2_t1",
     "d": "M 840 200 L 960 200 L 840 480 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq2_t2",
     "d": "M 960 200 L 960 480 L 840 480 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq2_t3",
     "d": "M 960 480 L 1240 480 L 1240 600 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "sq2_t4",
     "d": "M 960 480 L 960 600 L 1240 600 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 2,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq2_area_a",
     "x": 840,
     "y": 480,
     "w": 120,
     "h": 120,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq2_lbl_a2",
     "x": 900,
     "y": 525,
     "text": "a²",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq2_area_b",
     "x": 960,
     "y": 200,
     "w": 280,
     "h": 280,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sq2_lbl_b2",
     "x": 1100,
     "y": 325,
     "text": "b²",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Compare Remaining Areas",
   "say": "Both large frames have the same total area, and both contain four identical triangles. Remove the four blue triangles from both sides!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_left",
     "x": 360,
     "y": 640,
     "text": "Left Uncovered: c²",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eq_right",
     "x": 1040,
     "y": 640,
     "text": "Right Uncovered: a² + b²",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "comp_arrow",
     "x1": 530,
     "y1": 655,
     "x2": 850,
     "y2": 655,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": "both"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "comp_text",
     "x": 690,
     "y": 615,
     "text": "Same total area\n− 4 triangles",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Conclusion: a² + b² = c²",
   "say": "Because the remaining areas must be equal, a² + b² must equal c². That is why the Pythagorean theorem is always true.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_final",
     "x": 480,
     "y": 740,
     "w": 440,
     "h": 90,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "final_proof",
     "x": 700,
     "y": 760,
     "text": "a² + b² = c²",
     "size": 50,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}